# Project Structure

## Project: Delhi Urban Mobility Data Engineering Platform

This project uses Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 and Azure Databricks to build a data engineering pipeline using Delhi bus transit data.

## Architecture

```text
Delhi Bus Transit Data
        |
        v
Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2
        |
        |-- raw/
        |    |-- bus/
        |         |-- agency.txt
        |         |-- routes.txt
        |         |-- stops.txt
        |         |-- trips.txt
        |         |-- stop_times.txt
        |         |-- calendar.txt
        |         |-- fare_attributes.txt
        |
        v
Azure Databricks
        |
        |-- Bronze Layer
        |    |-- bronze_routes
        |    |-- bronze_stops
        |    |-- bronze_trips
        |    |-- bronze_stop_times
        |
        |-- Silver Layer
        |    |-- silver_routes
        |    |-- silver_stops
        |    |-- silver_trips
        |    |-- silver_stop_times
        |
        |-- Gold Layer
             |-- dim_route
             |-- dim_stop
             |-- dim_trip
             |-- fact_trip_stop
```

## Data Processing

- **Bronze:** Ingest raw transit data into Databricks tables.
- **Silver:** Clean and validate the data.
- **Gold:** Build dimensional tables and a fact table for analytics.

## Technologies

- Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2
- Azure Databricks
- PySpark
- SQL
- Delta Lake

## Analytics

The Gold layer supports analysis of routes, stops, trips, and stop occurrences using SQL.

